{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: siwa-product-card | Owner: A-02 | Task: ST-03

  P-01 ProductCard. The specimen on the shelf — lit, labelled, unadorned. Every
  grid, row and search result renders products through this one snippet, so the
  catalog stamp cannot be forgotten on one surface and remembered on another.

  THE STAMP IS NOT OPTIONAL. The media always asks siwa-catalog-badge, and that
  snippet decides between ORIGINAL, IMPRESSION and a loud untagged warning. A
  mixed grid without badges does not ship (non-negotiable 1).

  ALT TEXT IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, NOT A COURTESY.
  The audit found `alt` null on virtually every product image, so the fallback
  to product.title is what actually reaches a screen reader today. The ideal
  alt still describes the shot ("Oud Nights 50ml, amber glass bottle, front")
  and that copy belongs in Shopify's media library, not in this file.

  THE MARKDOWN TEST IS `compare_at > price`, NOT `compare_at EXISTS`.
  69 of 170 variants carry a junk compare_at_price of 0.0 from the import. Any
  card that treated a present compare_at as a markdown would put a red SALE
  stamp on 40% of the catalogue and turn the signal into noise.

  THE REFERENCE IS NEVER A BRAND LABEL.
  The eyebrow is the translated "Inspired by …" sentence and nothing else — no
  standalone vendor line, no brand name in the title, no "Inspired by" used as
  navigation. Originals get no eyebrow at all: a Siwa Original is inspired by
  nobody, and printing a reference on one would be a false claim. The vendor
  field is only read as a last resort and only when it is not the shop's own
  name, because the audit found the dupe reference parked there. The
  non-affiliation disclaimer that this framing depends on lives in the footer.

  STATUS STAMPS STACK OVER THE MEDIA, WITH THE CATALOG STAMP FIRST.
  siwa-components.css gives --overlay exactly one anchor, the inline-start
  corner, so a second --overlay badge would land on top of the catalog stamp
  and hide the one badge that may never be hidden. .siwa-card__badges — added
  in assets/siwa-product-card.css, which any section rendering a card must
  load — turns that single slot into a column. The catalog stamp is always
  first in the stack. Keeping status out of .siwa-card__body is also what
  holds the body to its four-element ceiling (CI warning 17).

  ONE LINK, ONE NAME. .siwa-card__link::after stretches over the whole card, so
  a second anchor inside it would be unreachable and would give the card two
  accessible names. Callers that need a wishlist control add it themselves at
  .siwa-card__wishlist, which sits above the stretched anchor on the z-ladder.

  Parameters
    product           required. Blank renders nothing.
    lazy              optional boolean, default true. Pass false for the cards
                      above the fold; everything below it stays lazy.
    show_price        optional boolean, default true.
    show_inspired_by  optional boolean, default true. Off for surfaces that are
                      already scoped to one reference.
    heading_level     optional, default 'h3'. The caller owns the document
                      outline — a card in an h2 section takes h3, a card under
                      an h3 takes h4. Anything outside h1–h6 falls back to h3.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign use_lazy = lazy | default: true, allow_false: true
  assign with_price = show_price | default: true, allow_false: true
  assign with_eyebrow = show_inspired_by | default: true, allow_false: true

  assign heading_tag = heading_level | default: 'h3' | downcase | strip
  assign heading_allowed = 'h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6' | split: ','
  unless heading_allowed contains heading_tag
    assign heading_tag = 'h3'
  endunless

  assign loading_mode = 'eager'
  if use_lazy
    assign loading_mode = 'lazy'
  endif

  comment
    The catalog line is resolved a second time here, by the same order
    siwa-catalog-badge uses, for one reason only: an Original must not carry an
    "Inspired by" eyebrow. The badge itself is still rendered by the snippet
    that owns it.
  endcomment
  assign catalog_line = ''
  assign reference = ''
  assign meta_path = settings.catalog_metafield | strip
  if meta_path contains '.'
    assign meta_parts = meta_path | split: '.'
    assign meta_namespace = meta_parts[0]
    assign meta_key = meta_parts[1]
    assign catalog_line = product.metafields[meta_namespace][meta_key].value | default: '' | downcase | strip
    assign reference = product.metafields[meta_namespace]["inspired_by"].value | default: '' | strip
  endif

  unless catalog_line == 'original' or catalog_line == 'impression'
    assign catalog_line = ''
    assign tag_original = settings.tag_original | downcase | strip
    assign tag_impression = settings.tag_impression | downcase | strip
    for product_tag in product.tags
      assign normalised_tag = product_tag | downcase | strip
      if tag_original != blank and normalised_tag == tag_original
        assign catalog_line = 'original'
        break
      endif
      if tag_impression != blank and normalised_tag == tag_impression
        assign catalog_line = 'impression'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endunless

  if reference == blank
    assign vendor_name = product.vendor | strip
    assign vendor_compare = vendor_name | downcase
    assign shop_compare = shop.name | downcase | strip
    if vendor_name != blank and vendor_compare != shop_compare
      assign reference = vendor_name
    endif
  endif

  assign show_reference = false
  if with_eyebrow and reference != blank and catalog_line != 'original'
    assign show_reference = true
  endif

  assign compare_at = product.compare_at_price_max | default: 0
  assign on_sale = false
  if compare_at > product.price_min
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  assign card_price = product.price_min | money
  assign card_alt = product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div class="siwa-card">
    <div class="siwa-card__media">
      <span class="siwa-card__badges">
        {%- render 'siwa-catalog-badge', product: product, overlay: true -%}
        {%- unless product.available -%}
          <span class="siwa-badge siwa-badge--soldout siwa-badge--overlay">
            {{- 'catalog.sold_out' | t -}}
          </span>
        {%- endunless -%}
        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <span class="siwa-badge siwa-badge--sale siwa-badge--overlay">
            {{- 'catalog.sale' | t -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>

      {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
        {{
          product.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 800
          | image_tag:
            alt: card_alt,
            loading: loading_mode,
            widths: '300, 450, 600, 800',
            sizes: '(max-width: 768px) 45vw, 300px'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="siwa-card__body">
      {%- if show_reference -%}
        <span class="siwa-card__eyebrow">
          {{- 'catalog.inspired_by' | t: reference: reference -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <{{ heading_tag }} class="siwa-card__title">
        <a class="siwa-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
      </{{ heading_tag }}>

      {%- if with_price -%}
        <span class="siwa-card__price">
          {%- if on_sale -%}
            <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.sale_price' | t }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if product.price_varies -%}
            {{ 'product.from_price' | t: price: card_price }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ card_price }}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if on_sale -%}
            <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.regular_price' | t }}</span>
            <span class="siwa-card__price-was">{{ compare_at | money }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
